NAME
       tty - print the terminal name

SYNOPSIS
       tty [-s]

DESCRIPTION
       Prints the name of the terminal on standard input.

OPTIONS
       -s     print nothing, only set the exit status

EXIT STATUS
       0 if standard input is a terminal, 1 otherwise. The underlying
       test is isatty, see stdio(3), on descriptor 0.

SEE ALSO
       csh(1)
